  "bmcuFreshTitle": "Red LEDs? Calibrate the buffers",
  "bmcuFreshSteps": "All 4 slots show the firmware default filament, a sign the BMCU memory was erased (BMCU Flasher erases everything when flashing). That erases the buffer calibration: until it is calibrated, the LEDs stay red and the motors do not turn. With no saved calibration the BMCU calibrates by itself at power-on, but only if no channel has filament.\n\n1. Remove filament from every channel (past the BMCU sensor). Make sure no broken piece is left inside.\n2. Turn the printer off and on without touching the buffers.\n3. The LEDs blink yellow for ~1 s while reading the rest position. If they blink red twice, filament is still in or a buffer moved: check and restart.\n4. When the channel LED blinks blue, push the buffer all the way in for 1 s and release.\n5. When it blinks red, pull it all the way out for 1 s and release.\n6. Repeat on the other channels (30 s per step) and leave everything released: two green blinks mean it saved.",
